FLUTTER BEST PRACTICE RULES (FOR RESPONSIVE, USER-FRIENDLY DEVELOPMENT)
🧠 GENERAL PRINCIPLES
Follow the Single Responsibility Principle (SRP)
Each widget or class should do one job only. Split UI logic from state and layout.

Use Meaningful, Consistent Naming
Stick to Dart conventions (camelCase for variables, PascalCase for widgets/classes).

Write Clean, Readable, and Formatted Code
Format with flutter format . or use your IDE’s formatter.

Comment Smartly
Comment why, not what—write self-explanatory code and add comments only for complex logic.

📱 RESPONSIVE UI RULES
Always Design for Responsiveness
Use MediaQuery, LayoutBuilder, or packages like flutter_screenutil or responsive_builder.

Avoid Fixed Width/Height — Use Flex Widgets
Use Flexible, Expanded, Wrap, or FittedBox for dynamic layout resizing.

Test on Multiple Screen Sizes
Simulate devices in Chrome dev tools or with different emulator sizes.

Wrap Content in SingleChildScrollView Where Needed
Prevent overflow and support scrolling on small screens.

Use SafeArea
Prevent UI collisions with system UI elements (notches, status bars).

🧩 REUSABLE COMPONENT RULES
Create Reusable Components (Widgets/Helpers)

Extract repeating widgets (e.g. buttons, form fields, containers).

Place reusable widgets in /widgets or /components folder.

Example: PrimaryButton, ResponsiveContainer, CustomTextField.

Use a Central TextStyle File
Create a text_styles.dart and define styles like:

dart
Copy
Edit
class AppTextStyles {
  static const heading = TextStyle(fontSize: 20, fontWeight: FontWeight.bold);
  static const body = TextStyle(fontSize: 16);
  static const label = TextStyle(fontSize: 14, color: Colors.grey);
}
Use a color_theme.dart for All Colors

dart
Copy
Edit
class AppColors {
  static const primary = Color(0xFF1A73E8);
  static const secondary = Color(0xFFFFA726);
  static const background = Color(0xFFF5F5F5);
  static const textDark = Color(0xFF212121);
}
Create a utilities.dart File

Add helper methods, reusable paddings, margins, validators, etc.

dart
Copy
Edit
class Utils {
  static EdgeInsets pagePadding = const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16, vertical: 20);
  static String capitalize(String text) => text[0].toUpperCase() + text.substring(1);
}
Theme Your App Consistently

Use ThemeData in main.dart:

dart
Copy
Edit
theme: ThemeData(
  primaryColor: AppColors.primary,
  textTheme: TextTheme(
    headline6: AppTextStyles.heading,
    bodyText2: AppTextStyles.body,
  ),
),
💡 UI/UX RULES
Consistent Theme & Typography

Touch Feedback: Use InkWell/GestureDetector with visual cues.

Inline & SnackBar Error Messages for user input.

Accessible & Legible Text Sizes with scalable font handling (MediaQuery.textScaleFactor if needed).

🔁 STATE MANAGEMENT & PERFORMANCE
Use const Where Possible
Improves performance by avoiding rebuilds.

Pick the Right State Management

Small apps: setState

Mid-large apps: Provider, Riverpod, GetX, Bloc, etc.

Dispose Controllers Properly
Always call .dispose() in StatefulWidget.

Don’t Rebuild Unnecessary Widgets
Use ValueListenableBuilder, Selector, or Consumer wisely.

📦 PACKAGES & DEPENDENCIES
Use Stable & Maintained Packages

Check version history, GitHub activity, and pub.dev score.

Audit Packages

Use flutter pub outdated to manage updates regularly.

Avoid Bloated Dependencies

Don’t install packages for tiny tasks that could be written with a few lines of Dart.

